One important principle: we should not jump directly to microservices. 
We'll first derive the architecture from requirements and scale, and at every major component 
I'll explain what it does, why we need it, why we choose it, how it works internally, 
when it is applicable, and when it is not.

That will make this a genuine L6 system-design upskilling program, 
rather than an Amazon architecture that you simply memorize.

